(vector (map (:adr/consequences "{:unambiguous_naming \"the compiler is once again named kami-engine-clj,\\n                        matching its pre-migration identity and removing the\\n                        'engine' vs 'kami-engine' vs 'kotoba-lang/engine'\\n                        naming confusion the user flagged\", :respects_no_rust_guard \"kami-engine's CI-enforced Rust-free invariant is\\n                            preserved -- this consolidation only works\\n                            because the compiler is genuinely Rust-free;\\n                            kami-clj-play/kami-script-runtime-rs's continued\\n                            separation is not incidental, it's required by\\n                            that same invariant\", :zero_broken_integrations \"kami-script-runtime-rs and kami-genre-base-\\n                              systems both still compile against the\\n                              (relocated) compiler; sequencing (copy+verify,\\n                              then update dependents, then archive old repo)\\n                              meant no window where a dependent pointed at a\\n                              dead/missing location\", :reversible_if_wrong \"archiving (not deleting) the old repo means this\\n                        decision can be cleanly reverted (unarchive, revert\\n                        the kami-engine PR, re-register in manifest) if it\\n                        turns out wrong, without any data loss\"}"), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "the CLJ->WASM compiler (built this session, ADR-2607031700) now lives at\n    orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-engine-clj, not at a standalone\n    orgs/kotoba-lang/engine repo -- that repo is archived (read-only, not\n    deleted) and its manifest/repos.edn + manifest/west.yml entries removed" "kami-clj-play and kami-script-runtime-rs (both contain real Rust source)\n    remain separate standalone kotoba-lang repos, unaffected by this move --\n    kami-engine's CI-enforced no-Rust guard is the reason they cannot join\n    kami-engine-clj there" "dependents' forward-pointing documentation (kami-script-runtime-rs,\n    kami-genre-base-systems, gftdcojp/isekai-network READMEs) now cite\n    kami-engine/kami-engine-clj; historical PR links (kotoba-lang/engine#1,\n    #2) are left unchanged since they remain valid, viewable citations on the\n    archived repo")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "kami-engine-clj-consolidation"), (:adr/related (vector "CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607010930-clj-wgsl-migration.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607031700-kotoba-lang-engine-wasm-emission-and-host-runtime.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607031800-kami-genre-base-systems.edn" "manifest/repos.edn" "manifest/west.yml" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #92 (merged)" "orgs/kotoba-lang/engine (archived)")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607032100-consolidate-engine-into-kami-engine-clj"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-03"), (:adr/body "# ADR 2607032100: consolidate kotoba-lang/engine into kami-engine/kami-engine-clj\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThe user flagged that \"engine\" alone doesn't read as a game engine and asked\nto organize it \"as kami-engine.\" The literal name collides with the existing\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine` repo (the original clj-wgsl-migration\nasset/contract home). Clarified via AskUserQuestion: consolidate only the\nRust-free piece into `kami-engine` as a subdirectory; leave `kami-clj-play`\nand `kami-script-runtime-rs` (both real Rust) as separate standalone repos,\nsince `kami-engine`'s CI enforces a repo-wide no-Rust guard — the same\ninvariant that made those two repos need to be standalone in the first\nplace.\n\n`kotoba-lang/engine` (this session's ADR-2607031700 CLJ→WASM compiler)\ncontains zero Rust source, confirmed by inspection and by its landing PR\npassing the no-rust guard check unmodified. `kami-engine` already hosts a mix\nof real `kami-*-clj` CLJC subdirectories and thin fixture-only directories\nsharing a name with a since-extracted crate (`kami-script-runtime/` inside\n`kami-engine` holds only a conformance-test fixture, not the real\nimplementation) — no `kami-engine-clj/` path existed yet, so this lands\nclean. The compiler's own pre-migration name, per `kami-engine`'s historical\ncrate table, was literally `kami-engine-clj` — consolidating under that name\nrestores the identity the clj-wgsl-migration extraction had temporarily\ndisplaced.\n\n## Decision\n\n### New home: `kami-engine/kami-engine-clj/`\n\nPlain copy of `kotoba-lang/engine`'s full content at its final commit\n`e8bb9afc7fd85f8ae044026f5a20c986d0bae42c` (not history-preserving, matching\nthis session's established precedent for repo moves). Provenance and the\nsource commit SHA recorded in `kami-engine-clj/PROVENANCE.md`. Verified in\nthe new location: `clojure -M:test` → 51 tests / 213 assertions, 0 failures\n— identical to the standalone repo, confirming the move changed nothing\nabout the code. Landed via `orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine` PR #92 (CI green,\nincluding the no-rust guard check), merged.\n\n### Old repo: archived, not deleted\n\n`kotoba-lang/engine`'s `README.edn` was updated to point at the new location,\nthen the repo was archived via the GitHub API (`archived=true`) — read-only,\nfully reversible, preserves history including PR #1/#2 for citation.\n`kami-clj-play` and `kami-script-runtime-rs` are unaffected: both contain\nreal Rust and correctly remain separate standalone repos, respecting\n`kami-engine`'s no-Rust CI guard. Neither was moved; `kami-script-runtime-rs`\nonly got a doc-link update pointing at the new compiler location.\n\n### Manifest cleanup\n\nRemoved the `\"orgs/kotoba-lang/engine\"` entry from `manifest/repos.edn`\n(commit `1619e2d52c4a546da97f7f6ec73ab1f2c19290d3`) and the corresponding\n`engine` project block from `manifest/west.yml` (commit\n`ed2f00acfd4382a2bfc45e900bde9ba1c4dfdcbf`), both via the established\nGitHub Contents API single-entry method. `kami-engine`'s own existing\nmanifest registration needed no change — this consolidation only adds a\nsubdirectory to its existing tree, not a new top-level project.\n\n### Dependent documentation updated\n\n- `kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs/README.edn` — forward-pointing intro\n  reference updated; historical PR #1/#2 links left as accurate citations\n  (still viewable on the archived repo).\n- `kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems/README.edn` — forward-pointing\n  verification-provenance reference updated; historical \"finding from this\n  pass\" narrative left as-is (it describes what was true when discovered,\n  not where to go today).\n- `gftdcojp/isekai-network/README.edn` — the \"WASM compile status\" section\n  had gone stale (it predated this session's compiler discovery, build, and\n  execution-verification work entirely, still describing \"no compiler\n  exists yet\"); rewritten to reflect the resolved state and the new\n  `kami-engine-clj` location. The \"Not yet done\" section's `kami-clj-play`\n  wiring note was similarly outdated and corrected.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The compiler is once again named `kami-engine-clj`, matching its\n  pre-migration identity and removing the \"engine\" vs \"kami-engine\" vs\n  \"kotoba-lang/engine\" naming confusion the user flagged.\n- `kami-engine`'s CI-enforced Rust-free invariant is preserved — this\n  consolidation only works because the compiler is genuinely Rust-free;\n  `kami-clj-play`/`kami-script-runtime-rs`'s continued separation isn't\n  incidental, it's required by that same invariant.\n- Zero broken integrations: sequencing (copy + verify, then update\n  dependents, then archive the old repo last) meant no window where a\n  dependent pointed at a dead location.\n- Reversible if wrong: archiving (not deleting) means this can be cleanly\n  reverted — unarchive, revert the `kami-engine` PR, re-register in\n  manifest — without data loss.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Rename `kotoba-lang/engine` to `kami-engine` (literal)**: rejected —\n   collides with the existing `kotoba-lang/kami-engine` repo.\n2. **Consolidate everything, including the real-Rust `kami-clj-play` and\n   `kami-script-runtime-rs`, into `kami-engine`**: rejected — would require\n   relaxing/removing `kami-engine`'s CI-enforced no-Rust guard, reversing a\n   deliberate migration decision (ADR-2607010930); the user explicitly\n   declined this via AskUserQuestion in favour of the Rust-free-only option.\n3. **Rename only (GitHub repo rename `kotoba-lang/engine` →\n   `kotoba-lang/kami-engine-clj`), without physically moving content**:\n   rejected — would leave the compiler as a fourth top-level `kotoba-lang`\n   repo alongside `kami-engine`/`kami-clj-play`/`kami-script-runtime-rs`\n   rather than actually organizing it *under* `kami-engine` as asked; only\n   relabels the problem instead of resolving where it belongs.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607010930 (clj-wgsl migration — the extraction this consolidation\n  partially reverses, and the source of `kami-engine`'s no-Rust guard)\n- ADR-2607031700 (kotoba-lang/engine's WASM emission and host runtime — the\n  work this ADR relocates)\n- ADR-2607031800 (kami-genre-base-systems — a dependent whose docs were\n  updated here)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine` PR #92 (merged)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/engine` (archived)"), (:adr/decision "{:new_path {:repo \"orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine\", :subdir \"kami-engine-clj/\", :method \"plain copy of kotoba-lang/engine's full content (src/,\\n                      test/, deps.edn, README.edn, LICENSE) at its final\\n                      commit e8bb9afc7fd85f8ae044026f5a20c986d0bae42c,\\n                      matching this session's established plain-copy\\n                      precedent for repo moves (not history-preserving).\\n                      Provenance + source commit SHA recorded in\\n                      kami-engine-clj/PROVENANCE.md.\", :verified \"clojure -M:test in the new location: 51 tests / 213\\n                        assertions, 0 failures -- identical to the standalone\\n                        repo's own count, confirming the move changed nothing\\n                        about the code itself\", :landed_via \"orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #92, CI green (the\\n                          no-rust guard check specifically), merged\"}, :old_repo {:repo \"orgs/kotoba-lang/engine\", :action \"README updated to point at the new location, then\\n                      archived via the GitHub API (archived=true) -- NOT\\n                      deleted. Archiving is read-only and reversible\\n                      (unarchive), preserving full history including PR #1/#2\\n                      for citation.\", :unaffected \"kami-clj-play and kami-script-runtime-rs -- both\\n                          contain real Rust and correctly remain separate\\n                          standalone repos, respecting kami-engine's no-Rust\\n                          CI guard. Not moved, not touched beyond a doc-link\\n                          update in kami-script-runtime-rs's README.\"}, :manifest_update {:repos_edn \"removed the \\\"orgs/kotoba-lang/engine\\\" line via GitHub\\n               Contents API single-entry PUT (blob-sha-matched against\\n               origin/main tip), commit 1619e2d52c4a546da97f7f6ec73ab1f2c19290d3\", :west_yml \"removed the 'engine' project entry (name/remote/revision/path/\\n              groups, 5 lines) via the same API method, commit\\n              ed2f00acfd4382a2bfc45e900bde9ba1c4dfdcbf\", :kami_engine_entry \"kami-engine's own existing west.yml/repos.edn\\n                       registration needed no change -- it was already\\n                       registered from the original clj-wgsl migration; this\\n                       consolidation only adds a subdirectory to its existing\\n                       tree, not a new top-level project\"}, :dependent_docs_updated [\"orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs README.edn (forward-pointing intro\\n    reference; historical PR #1/#2 links left as accurate citations)\" \"orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems README.edn (forward-pointing\\n    verification-provenance reference; historical 'finding from this pass'\\n    narrative left as-is)\" \"orgs/gftdcojp/isekai-network README.edn (updated the now-stale 'WASM\\n    compile status' section, which had predated this session's compiler\\n    discovery/build/verification work entirely -- also fixed the outdated\\n    kami-clj-play wiring note in the 'Not yet done' section)\"]}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/problem "{:source \"user request 2026-07-03: 'engine だけだと game engine とわからないので、kami-engine として整理したいかな' (the bare name 'engine' doesn't read as a game engine, wants it organized under kami-engine), then, after being shown that the literal name kami-engine already exists as a different repo, clarified via AskUserQuestion: consolidate only the Rust-free piece into kami-engine as a subdirectory, leave the Rust-containing repos (kami-clj-play, kami-script-runtime-rs) separate\", :investigated [\"kami-engine's own CI enforces a repo-wide no-Rust guard (confirmed via\\n    its CLAUDE.md and the passing 'WIT single-source + no-rust guard' check\\n    on the landing PR) -- this guard is the direct reason kami-script-\\n    runtime-rs (real Rust, wasmtime/wgpu) had to become its own standalone\\n    repo in the first place, per this session's earlier recovery work\" \"kotoba-lang/engine (this session's ADR-2607031700 compiler) contains\\n    zero Rust source -- verified by inspection before the move, and by the\\n    landing PR's own CI passing the no-rust guard check unmodified\" \"kami-engine already hosts a mix of real kami-*-clj CLJC subdirectories\\n    (kami-app-sip-clj, kami-mangaka-*-clj, etc.) and thin fixture-only\\n    directories with the same historical name as a since-extracted crate\\n    (kami-script-runtime/ inside kami-engine holds only tests/survivors.clj,\\n    a conformance fixture, not the real implementation which lives in the\\n    separate kami-script-runtime and kami-script-runtime-rs repos) -- no\\n    kami-engine-clj/ path existed yet, so this consolidation is a clean\\n    landing, not a collision with existing fixture content\" \"the compiler's own pre-migration name (per kami-engine's historical\\n    CLAUDE.md crate table, already in this session's context) was literally\\n    kami-engine-clj -- consolidating back under that name restores the\\n    original, unambiguous naming this session's clj-wgsl-migration-driven\\n    extraction had temporarily lost\"], :risk \"kotoba-lang/engine was a live, public, already-integrated-with repo\\n         (kami-script-runtime-rs and kami-genre-base-systems both compile\\n         against it, isekai-network's README documented it) -- archiving it\\n         without first landing the content elsewhere and updating dependents\\n         would have broken those integrations; sequenced as copy-and-verify\\n         first, archive last, to avoid that\"}"), (:adr/alternatives "[{:option \"rename kotoba-lang/engine to kami-engine (literal)\", :rejected_because \"collides with the existing orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine\\n                       repo (the original clj-wgsl-migration asset/contract\\n                       home) -- not a valid name\"} {:option \"consolidate everything (including kami-clj-play and\\n            kami-script-runtime-rs, both real Rust) into kami-engine\", :rejected_because \"would require relaxing/removing kami-engine's CI-\\n                       enforced no-Rust guard, reversing a deliberate,\\n                       carefully-executed migration decision (ADR-2607010930)\\n                       -- explicitly declined by the user via AskUserQuestion\\n                       in favour of the Rust-free-only option\"} {:option \"rename only, without physically moving the content (e.g. a repo-\\n            level GitHub rename kotoba-lang/engine -> kotoba-lang/kami-engine-clj)\", :rejected_because \"would leave the compiler as a fourth top-level\\n                       kotoba-lang repo alongside kami-engine, kami-clj-play,\\n                       kami-script-runtime-rs, rather than actually\\n                       organizing it under kami-engine as the user asked --\\n                       doesn't address the underlying 'where does this\\n                       belong' question, only the label\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607032100: consolidate kotoba-lang/engine into kami-engine/kami-engine-clj"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))